  "note": "Capability 89, contract/ext-bots-v1.md row 89. A chat client declares a bot's REMOTE MCP servers on the capability-48 bot_config profile.write, forwarded only to a peer that negotiated the attach-v1 capability mcp_server_declarations. transport is the literal http: no stdio shape exists. A header value names one COZY_MCP_ environment variable, never a value, and the peer expands it only for a url origin the operator listed in COZY_MCP_<NAME>_ORIGINS. The gateway refuses userinfo, query, fragment, backslash, placeholders and literal loopback, link-local and metadata hosts; the peer's url policy owns resolved addresses, .local and private hosts (a separate operator opt-in) and redirects. Every tool of a client-declared server asks. A declared row is projected back read-only as BotMcpServer.declaration, closed: growing it needs a new capability.",
